  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Lakewood Hills is the White Bear Lake favorite — a front nine of rolling hills and trees, a back nine that goes fully wooded, and dual tees on most holes that let every level find their distance. From the standard pins it plays 4,391 feet at par 54.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Chainstar baskets, it's the kind of course where a putter and a midrange are almost enough — and where the back nine's woods quietly demand your full attention.",
    "Quick, friendly, and endlessly replayable: a lunch-break loop that locals never tire of."
  ],
